From: JorreFog <JorreFog@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gfx/drm_ctx: fast-forward with two swapchain images

With video_max_swapchain_images = 2 the KMS context waited for every page
flip, even in nonblocking mode (swap interval 0), so fast-forward could not
run faster than the display refresh. Skip that wait when the interval is 0
and GBM has a free buffer, as the triple-buffered path already does.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/gfx/drivers_context/drm_ctx.c	2026-10-18 03:56:00.835038675 +0200
+++ b/gfx/drivers_context/drm_ctx.c	2026-10-18 03:56:00.842112520 +0200
@@ -600,6 +600,14 @@
          && gbm_surface_has_free_buffers(drm->gbm_surface))
       return;
 
+   /* Nonblocking (interval 0: fast-forward) with two images too: don't wait
+    * for the flip here, the next swap drops its frame while one is pending.
+    * Otherwise every frame waits for vblank and fast-forward never goes
+    * faster than the display. */
+   if (     !drm->interval
+         && gbm_surface_has_free_buffers(drm->gbm_surface))
+      return;
+
    gfx_ctx_drm_wait_flip(drm, true);
 }
 
